py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AUxpoQqaJc3seofWjooHbM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PCy45fqHUuraE29odbyQ9E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the change is merged into main, so it should go out in today's release.\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding, but the code actually rounded halves up. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: it expects 2.665 to round to 2.66.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created the branch `fix/money-round-half-even` and changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding. That was the only change.\n2. Ran CI on that commit (run `ci-0001`), and it passed.\n3. Opened pull request #101 against main. The code-owner wasn't added as a reviewer when the PR was created, so I requested their review separately.\n4. Merged PR #101. The merge went to the code-owner for approval first, as policy requires, and they approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\").\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. The fix follows the test and the code's own description, which both call for banker's rounding.", "type": "text"}]}]}